{"book":"1nephi","colophon":{"en":"An account of Lehi and his wife Sariah, and his four sons, being called, (beginning at the eldest) Laman, Lemuel, Sam, and Nephi. The Lord warns Lehi to depart out of the land of Jerusalem, because he prophesieth unto the people concerning their iniquity and they seek to destroy his life. He taketh three days' journey into the wilderness with his family. Nephi taketh his brethren and returneth to the land of Jerusalem after the record of the Jews. The account of their sufferings. They take the daughters of Ishmael to wife. They take their families and depart into the wilderness. Their sufferings and afflictions in the wilderness. The course of their travels. They come to the large waters. Nephi's brethren rebel against him. He confoundeth them, and buildeth a ship. They call the name of the place Bountiful. They cross the large waters into the promised land, and so forth. This is according to the account of Nephi; or in other words, I, Nephi, wrote this record.","sm":"O se tala ia Liae ma lana ava o Sarai, ma ona atalii e toafa, e igoa (e amata mai i le ulumatua) ia Lamana, Lemuelu, Sama, ma Nifae. Ua lapataia Liae e le Alii ia alu ese atu mai le laueleele o Ierusalema, ona sa vavalo atu o ia i tagata e uiga i lo latou amioletonu ma ua latou saili ai e faaumatia lona ola. Ua malaga atu o ia i le vao i aso e tolu faatasi ma lona aiga. Ua ave e Nifae ona uso ma foi atu i le laueleele o Ierusalema ina ia maua mai le talafaamaumau o tagata Iutaia. O le tala i o latou mafatiaga. Ua latou ave afafine o Isamaeli ma faiavā i ai. Ua latou ave o latou aiga ma o ese atu i le vao. O o latou mafatiaga ma puapuaga i le vao. O le ala na ui ai la latou malaga. Ua latou tau atu i vai tetele. Ua fouvale uso o Nifae ia te ia. Ua ia faafememeaiina i laua, ma fausia se vaa. Ua latou faaigoaina le nofoaga o Nuumau. Ua latou sopo atu i vai tetele i le laueleele na folafolaina, ma isi mea. O lenei ua tusa ai ma le tala a Nifae; po o i ni isi upu, o a'u, o Nifae, na tusia lenei tala.","words":[{"en":"·","sm":"O"},{"en":"·","sm":"se"},{"en":"·","sm":"tala"},{"en":"·","sm":"ia"},{"en":"An account of Lehi","sm":"Liae"},{"en":"·","sm":"ma"},{"en":"·","sm":"lana"},{"en":"·","sm":"ava"},{"en":"·","sm":"o"},{"en":"and his wife Sariah,","sm":"Sarai,"},{"en":"·","sm":"ma"},{"en":"·","sm":"ona"},{"en":"·","sm":"atalii"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"and his four sons,","sm":"toafa,"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"being called","sm":"igoa"},{"en":"·","sm":"(e"},{"en":"·","sm":"amata"},{"en":"·","sm":"mai"},{"en":"·","sm":"i"},{"en":"·","sm":"le"},{"en":"(beginning at the eldest)","sm":"ulumatua)"},{"en":"·","sm":"ia"},{"en":"·","sm":"Lamana,"},{"en":"Laman, Lemuel,","sm":"Lemuelu,"},{"en":"·","sm":"Sama,"},{"en":"·","sm":"ma"},{"en":"Sam, and Nephi.","sm":"Nifae."},{"en":"·","sm":"Ua"},{"en":"·","sm":"lapataia"},{"en":"·","sm":"Liae"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"·","sm":"le"},{"en":"The Lord warns Lehi","sm":"Alii"},{"en":"·","sm":"ia"},{"en":"·","sm":"alu"},{"en":"·","sm":"ese"},{"en":"to depart","sm":"atu"},{"en":"·","sm":"mai"},{"en":"·","sm":"le"},{"en":"·","sm":"laueleele"},{"en":"·","sm":"o"},{"en":"out of the land of Jerusalem,","sm":"Ierusalema,"},{"en":"·","sm":"ona"},{"en":"·","sm":"sa"},{"en":"·","sm":"vavalo"},{"en":"·","sm":"atu"},{"en":"·","sm":"o"},{"en":"because he prophesied","sm":"ia"},{"en":"·","sm":"i"},{"en":"unto the people","sm":"tagata"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"·","sm":"uiga"},{"en":"concerning","sm":"i"},{"en":"·","sm":"lo"},{"en":"·","sm":"latou"},{"en":"their iniquity","sm":"amioletonu"},{"en":"·","sm":"ma"},{"en":"·","sm":"ua"},{"en":"·","sm":"latou"},{"en":"·","sm":"saili"},{"en":"and they sought","sm":"ai"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"·","sm":"faaumatia"},{"en":"·","sm":"lona"},{"en":"to destroy his life.","sm":"ola."},{"en":"·","sm":"Ua"},{"en":"·","sm":"malaga"},{"en":"·","sm":"atu"},{"en":"·","sm":"o"},{"en":"He journeys","sm":"ia"},{"en":"·","sm":"i"},{"en":"·","sm":"le"},{"en":"into the wilderness"